## B. Correct interaction flow

The expected workflow:

1. User presses the microphone button.
2. JARVIS starts listening.
3. User speaks.
4. User releases or stops the microphone.
5. Speech recognition completes.
6. JARVIS processes the recognized request.
7. JARVIS returns its response.
8. Text-to-speech speaks the response if enabled.
9. Microphone remains inactive until the user presses the button again.

Do not process partial speech as a completed request unless the selected recognition engine explicitly supports a deliberate streaming mode.

## C. Eliminate self-listening and feedback loops

